/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (A sustainable cultural economy ensures the long-term viability of cultural practices, provides economic benefits to local communities, notably vulnerable groups, and offers visitors unique and authentic experiences. By investing in and supporting CCIs, local governments can create stable and fairly paid jobs and contribute to the sustainable development of the tourism sector. The establishment of comprehensive local strategies allows cities to prioritize cultural projects and tourism marketing by encouraging cooperation between the public and private sectors and local communities. In addition to adding economic value, GI for cultural offers can also reduce the risk of heritage exploitation associated with, for example, crafts, textiles and food products, and promote its sustainable development.13)
/E (A sustainable cultural economy ensures the long-term viability of cultural practices, provides economic benefits to local communities, notably vulnerable groups, and offers visitors unique and authentic experiences. By investing in and supporting CCIs, local governments can create stable and fairly paid jobs and contribute to the sustainable development of the tourism sector. The establishment of comprehensive local strategies allows cities to prioritize cultural projects and tourism marketing by encouraging cooperation between the public and private sectors and local communities. In addition to adding economic value, GI for cultural offers can also reduce the risk of heritage exploitation associated with, for example, crafts, textiles and food products, and promote its sustainable development.13)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [9 10]
>>
