<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Cultural education and inter-cultural exchanges promote mutual understanding, preserve cultural heritage, and enhance the visitor experience. Museums and cultural centres play a vital role by providing spaces where local history, traditions, and contemporary culture are showcased, experienced and transmitted. Training professionals, promoting regular exchanges between the public and private sectors and local communities, and learning from the examples of other cities can improve urban planning and sustainable tourism development strategies. In general, cultural education and training are crucial for both local communities and tourists, fostering a sense of respect and appreciation for cultural diversity in the local settings. This approach helps to create a more inclusive, informed, and cohesive community, ultimately leading to more sustainable and enriching tourism experiences.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [9]
>>
