285 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Digital innovation improves and diversifies access to cultural resources, supports community engagement, and provides new avenues for tourism actors, including destinations, businesses, and cultural institutions. It also enhances inclusivity by improving accessibility for vulnerable groups, ensuring their participation in cultural and tourism activities within cities. Embracing digital transformation, harnessing technology, and using social media effectively and responsibly, are key to modernizing tourism and improving the visitor experience. In addition, social media has become a primary communication tool; using it effectively to attract visitors and raise their awareness is key to sustainable tourism. Local governments and communities, including the private sector, can leverage big data and algorithms to refine tourism strategies, optimize marketing efforts, and improve the visitor experiences. In parallel, new technologies such as virtual reality and augmented reality, and more recently artificial intelligence, offer innovative ways to enrich tourism offerings, providing immersive and interactive experiences that can attract a wider audience. These technologies not only enhance the visitor experience, but also contribute to accessibility and sustainability by reducing the need for physical travel and minimizing the environmental impact.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
