309 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The Superblock programme has been developed and consolidated as an international benchmark urban intervention. This initiative aims to make the city of Barcelona more sustainable by reducing vehicle circulation in favour of pedestrians, creating green spaces, promoting sustainable mobility and creating spaces where cultural events, such as concerts or shows, can take place in the neighbourhoods, thanks to strategically located electricity and energy points. Currently, Barcelona counts thirteen Superblocks and plans on expanding the model to an increasing number of spaces. As a city facing increasing tourism flows, Barcelona is using the Superblock initiative to create sustainable and diverse cultural options for locals and visitors.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [1]
>>
